description:
The full list of dependencies is not installable on Ubuntu 20 nor Ubuntu 22.

Expectation: to install every dependency for all the packages available on CRAN.
Actual: One R package is not installable, or the dependencies will switch each time they are re-installed.

The following packages conflict:

Requires `libcurl4-openssl-dev`:
- {nucim}
- {strawr}
- {cogmapr}
- {bioimagetools}
- {RCurl}
- {mRpostman}
- {arrow}
- {curl}

Requires `librdf0-dev` requires `librasqal3-dev` requires `libraptor2-dev` requires `libcurl4-gnutls-dev` conflicts `libcurl4-openssl-dev`:
- {redland}

Options to resolve conflict:
1. Update `libraptor2-dev` package in the Ubuntu PPAs
2. Install `libcurl4-gnutls-dev` instead of `libcurl4-openssl-dev` as the dependency of all 8 packages above, for the sake of a single R package.

I'm not sure if the 8 R packages are compatible with the GnuTLS variant but I would expect them to be.

Does anyone have any experience with the `libcurl` variants available on Ubuntu?

I don't think changing the dependencies in this database for all 8 packages is necessarily sensible but it does resolve this issue.
